// Pull request: #6426 New Rule: Suspicious Child Process Spawned By IntelliTrace.EXE
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6426
// Pull request author: Diablo-research
// Change: new rule
// Title: Suspicious Child Process Spawned By IntelliTrace.EXE
// Sigma ID: ecc8eb3a-d52a-4a63-8e38-f81e31285eed
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Nazar Diachok (@Diablo-research)
// Date: 2026-10-04 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1127
// Description: Detects suspicious command and script interpreters spawned by the Microsoft Visual Studio
//   IntelliTrace utility. IntelliTrace supports launching an arbitrary executable for diagnostic
//   tracing and may be abused to proxy execution through a Microsoft-signed developer utility.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate Visual Studio diagnostic workflows that intentionally trace command or script interpreters
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/IntelliTrace/
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/visualstudio/debugger/intellitrace
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/3a3ad068d3dd62c9f86645824580003e1e026268/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_intellitrace_susp_child.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\IntelliTrace.exe" and (FolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\cscript.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\mshta.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\wscript.exe")
